## Project layout

```
ollavoice/
├── install-windows.bat          double-click installer
├── scripts/setup.ps1            Windows installer (venv, packages, models, shortcuts)
├── scripts/setup.sh             Linux/macOS installer
├── scripts/build-windows-exe.ps1  PyInstaller build of OllaVoice.exe
├── packaging/OllaVoice.spec
├── run_gui.py                   entry point for the frozen exe
├── docs/                        INSTALL-windows, ARCHITECTURE, TROUBLESHOOTING
├── tests/                       250+ tests incl. real Piper+Whisper round trips
└── ollavoice/
    ├── cli.py  repl.py  server.py  setup.py
    ├── pipeline.py              mic -> Whisper -> Ollama -> TTS orchestration
    ├── config.py  hardware.py  paths.py  downloads.py  voices.py
    ├── stt_engines.py           faster-whisper / whisper.cpp / ollama / windows
    ├── tts_engines.py           piper / kokoro / sapi / silent
    ├── vad.py  textsplit.py  wav.py  audioio.py  ollama_client.py
    ├── gui/                     main_window, settings_dialog, workers, hotkeys, theme
    └── server/static/           the browser UI
```

See [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) for how the pieces fit
together, and [docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md](docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md) when something
misbehaves.

---

## Development

```bash
pip install -e ".[all]" pytest ruff
pytest -q                              # 250+ tests, no downloads, no audio hardware
OLLAVOICE_IT=1 pytest -q               # + real Piper/Whisper round trips
ruff check . --select=F,E9 --preview
```

The GUI tests run against a permissive fake `PySide6` when Qt cannot load
([`tests/qt_stub/`](tests/qt_stub/__init__.py)), so they work in headless CI and
still catch typos, bad imports and construction-time errors. With real Qt
installed they construct the actual window on the `offscreen` platform.

